\paragraph{Splitting rules.} Folds are formed as in Section~\ref{sec:robustness:methods}: no group is split, and classification folds are stratified with a fixed seed. Every dataset uses five outer folds. No split is random, because random splitting inflates performance estimates for molecular data by placing structurally similar compounds on both sides of the train/test boundary \citep{Yang2019, Wallach2018}. On a given dataset, every representation, model and hybrid is scored on the same folds.

