In the Koenig deep mutational scan of the anti-vascular endothelial growth factor (VEGF) antibody G6, each variant carries one mutation. Variants are grouped by the mutated position modulo 5, as in ProteinGym \citep{Notin2023}, giving five folds of 836 to 874 variants, so a model cannot look up a per-position effect at test time \citep{Vieira2026}. The nanobody and humanness sets are grouped by single-linkage clusters at 95\% sequence identity, after \citet{Kenlay2024}. The trastuzumab variants differ from the wild type only in the ten residues of CDR-H3 and are grouped by how many of them are mutated.

