% TODO: review, needs manual review
\paragraph{\texorpdfstring{hERG $K_i$.}{hERG Ki.}} hERG records (ChEMBL target CHEMBL240) were retrieved from ChEMBL \citep{Zdrazil2023}, keeping binding assays (assay type B) with standard type $K_i$, a pChEMBL value, an exact relation (``$=$'') and no curator data-validity comment. The label is the pChEMBL value, $\mathrm{p}K_i = -\log_{10} K_i$ with $K_i$ in molar units. Repeat measurements of one compound are merged into their median, and compounds whose repeats have a standard deviation above 1.0 p$K_i$ unit are removed, following \citet{landrum2024}. This gives 1,415 compounds, 226 of them measured more than once and none removed by the standard-deviation rule. After standardization, InChIKey deduplication removes 3, leaving 1,412 compounds with p$K_i$ from 4.07 to 9.41. The same query against ChEMBL release 37 reproduces the file used.

